309	98,476,787,895 - 640,745,790,897	309. Half of a flower of the common Purslane, divided lengthwise and magnified.	A Purslane flower cut in half: spreading petals, a row of stamens, and the style branches above the ovary, which is sunk in the dotted calyx and shows its seeds inside.
310	126,985,380,1340	310. Pod of the same, opening by a lid.	The Purslane pod split round the middle, its pointed top lifted off like a lid to show the heap of seeds in the cup below.
311	540,460,1605,1345 - 535,455,790,745 - 805,1140,1610,1350	311. Claytonia or Spring-Beauty.	A whole plant rising on a long slender stem from a small rounded tuber, with one pair of long narrow leaves and a loose raceme of five-petalled flowers and buds.
312	810,1145,985,1340	312 Its 2-cleft calyx and pod.	The two broad sepals of the calyx on a short stalk, clasping the pod that shows between them.
313	1035,1185,1150,1335	313. Ripe pod cut across, and splitting into three valves.	The ripe pod with its walls parting into three valves and a few round seeds showing inside.
314	1200,1210,1310,1325	314. Seed, more magnified.	A single round, flattened seed, its surface covered with small dots.
315	1355,1210,1455,1325	315. Same, cut through, to show the coiled embryo.	The seed cut through, showing the slender embryo curled in a ring round the albumen.
316	1505,1235,1590,1315	316. Embryo taken out.	The embryo alone: a slender body bent into a hook-shaped coil.
